  "query_preview": "..\n\nSustained winds have been approaching 30 mph with gusts near 40\nmph across Fort Peck Lake overnight. Hi res models have more\npersistent east to southeast winds across NE Montana than the NBM,\nguiding through Tuesday morning. Thus, have issued a Lake Wind\nAdvisory for Fort Peck Lake. Secondarily, look for isolated\nshowers over the SE zones on Monday as low pressure tracks well\nsouth and east of the region, though cloud cover will extend area\nwide.\n\nEnsembles show an upper trough extending east into the middle of\nthe week, leading to increasing chances for rainfall. QPF\nforecasts have trended lower this cycle, but remain between a\n0.10\" and 0.25\" over most areas. Look for lesser amounts toward\nthe MT/ND border.\n\nAside from occasional precipitation chances, below average\ntemperatures will also take the stage through most of this week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was focused for most elements this forecast cycle, though a\nlittle blend toward high resolution mesoscale models was\nimplemented for near term winds in support of the Fort Peck Lake\nWind Advisory and consistent with trending observations for those\nsurrounding areas. Otherwise, confidence remains above average on\ncool and unsettled weather for the middle of the week, though\nuncertainty remains on specific amounts.",
